# ── Dependencies ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# ── Build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
dist/
gen/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Secrets — NEVER commit ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa
id_ed25519
.npmrc

# ── Midnight / NIGHTGATE local state ──────────────────────────────────────────
private-state-db/
.midnight/
zk-artifacts/
*.sqlite
*.db

# Compiled Compact output: contract/, compiler/ and zkir/ ARE committed, so
# judges and consumers can inspect the build without a Compact toolchain —
# NIGHTGATE's own convention. PLONK prover/verifier keys are large and fully
# regenerable, so those stay out.
**/managed/**/keys/

# ── Salt seeds ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are proof openings. Publishing one undoes leaf salting; losing one makes
# an anchored root permanently unprovable. Back them up OUT OF BAND, never here.
seeds/
*.seed

# ── Local-only material (see docs/DECISIONS.md) ───────────────────────────────
patent/
Midnight Build Club/
Archive - GitHub Repos*/

# ── Local-only tracking — security backlog and open issues ────────────────────
# Canonical copies live OUTSIDE this repo at ../_local-tracking/. These patterns
# are a second line of defence in case one is ever created in the tree.
# GitHub Issues/Wiki/Projects are disabled on this repo by design.
_local/
_local-tracking/
*.local.md
OPEN-ISSUES.md
SECURITY-BACKLOG.md

# Throwaway chain/wallet probes. They are written against real preprod state and
# routinely hold an address, a job id or a hand-pasted key while being debugged,
# so they must never reach a public remote. Kept structural rather than relying
# on remembering to list paths on every commit.
scripts/spike-*.mjs

# ── Editor / OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
private/

# ── Security notes — LOCAL ONLY, never committed ──────────────────────────────
# Standing rule: security findings and open issues are tracked locally, not in
# a public repository, and not in commit messages either. Anything matching
# these patterns stays on the machine it was written on.
SECURITY-NOTES.local.md
*.local.md
security-notes/
